UNIT ringLabel
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY spec
SIG ringLabel(items: array, gate) -> Promise<array>
DESCRIPTION Takes an array of items and produces an array of formatted strings, one per item. Each actor (indexed 0 to n-1) produces exactly one string: the string "<index>:<item>" for its own position in the input array.
DESCRIPTION The token circulates: actor 0 takes the token first, formats its item as a string, and passes the token to actor 1. Actor i (for 0 < i < n-1) receives the token from actor i-1, formats its item as a string, and passes to actor i+1. Actor n-1 receives the token, formats its item as a string, and releases the token.
DESCRIPTION The unit computes the string formatting itself (concatenating index and item with a colon separator). The gate provides only mutual exclusion: the token is held in gate.token, and the unit calls gate.token.take(who) to acquire it, gate.token.pass(from, to) to transfer it, and gate.token.release(who) to release it.
DESCRIPTION The output array preserves input order: output[i] is the formatted string for items[i], for all i in [0, n-1].
DESCRIPTION If the input array is empty, the unit returns an empty array without acquiring or releasing the token.
RING Token circulates 0 → 1 → 2 → ... → (n-1) → release. Each actor in index order takes the token, performs its formatting work, and passes to the next actor. The final actor releases the token.
INVARIANT At most one actor holds the token at any instant. No two actors may call gate.token.take or gate.token.pass concurrently (mutual exclusion enforced by the gate).
INVARIANT The token is taken exactly n times (once per actor i=0..n-1) and released exactly once by actor n-1. No token is lost or duplicated.
INVARIANT The returned array contains exactly n strings, in index order. For each i in [0, n-1], output[i] == "<i>:<items[i]>" (the string representation of the item at position i, prefixed by the index and a colon).
INVARIANT Actors acquire the token in strict index order: actor i+1 may not call gate.token.take until actor i has called gate.token.pass(i, i+1).
INVARIANT When items is empty, the unit returns an empty array without invoking gate.token.
